    "body": "It looks like for some reason `starship` is not in your `Path` when PowerShell runs in Windows Terminal. You can work around this by replacing `starship` in your PowerShell `$PROFILE` with an absolute path to the starship binary (`Invoke-Expression (& C:\\path\\to\\starship.exe init powershell)`) or adding its file location to the search path dynamically first (`$env:Path += \";C:\\path\\to\\`). You can also consult the Windows settings to ensure the directory with starship listed in the `Path` variable.\r\n\r\nPlease re-open this issue if my comments haven't solved your issue.",
